    "narrative": "Today\u2019s offensive outlook for the Austin Waves is headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), both of whom benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Miles Mikolas and Brandon Young, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our highest-upside play, utilizing a massive +17% SP skill advantage and a +14% boost from a dynamic platoon split, cementing his status as a must-start at SS. **Josh Lowe** (72.21) also vaults into the top tier today; despite the \"Lineup Pending\" status, he draws Roki Sasaki, whose 5.23 xERA is the most exploitable mark on the slate. The combination of an elite SP skill boost (+19%) and a significant platoon advantage makes **Josh Lowe** an excellent value play at OF3, even if he hits lower in the order.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Sam Antonacci** (54.41), who narrowly missed the cut for the final utility spot. While his xwOBA is an elite 0.378, he was squeezed out by **Nolan Schanuel** (61.46) and **Dominic Smith** (56.54), who benefited from more favorable park factors and the optimizer\u2019s preference for the specific platoon alignments available in their matchups. **Sam Antonacci** fell victim to a -5% wind-in warning at his venue, which mitigated his raw power upside. Owners should monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Nasim Nunez**, and **Brady House**; while they are projected for strong starts, the confirmed batting order is vital to sustaining their efficiency scores. **Jackson Merrill** (56.83) warrants a cautious watch as he draws the toughest arm of the day in George Kirby (3.45 xERA), and while his floor remains stable, he lacks the ceiling of our top-tier hitters if the game turns into a pitcher\u2019s duel.",
